    defEn: 'Egyptian expression meaning "in peace". <i>Em</i> (transliterated <i>m</i>) is the preposition "in"; <i>hotep</i> (<i>ḥtp</i>) means "peace, contentment, satisfaction" and also "offering" (Faulkner, 1962). It figured in greeting and farewell formulas, such as "come in peace" and "go in peace". That is how it serves today as a greeting, roughly "be at peace". The vocalization "em hotep" is conventional: Egyptian writing did not record vowels.'
