    defEn: 'Funerary god with a jackal head, lord of embalming and guide of the dead on the path to judgment. The peasant\'s name, Khun-Anup, means "protected of Anubis", and it is to him that the peasant threatens to appeal when he loses faith in human justice, at the close of the ninth petition.'
